  "notes": "Composed of {平|へい} (flat, peaceful) and {定|てい} (settle, establish). Implies restoring peace through military force. Primarily used in historical contexts, especially accounts of feudal Japan and military campaigns.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {反乱|はんらん}を{平定|へいてい}する: to suppress a rebellion\n- {全国|ぜんこく}{平定|へいてい}: national unification by force\n- {領土|りょうど}を{平定|へいてい}する: to pacify a territory\n- {内乱|ないらん}の{平定|へいてい}: suppression of a civil war\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {鎮圧|ちんあつ}: suppression — focuses on putting down by force, often used for riots and uprisings\n- {征服|せいふく}: conquest — emphasizes the act of conquering\n- {征伐|せいばつ}: subjugation, punitive expedition — military campaign to punish and subdue",
